.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH analyze 1  "analyze " 
.SH NAME
analyze \- Mine shell history for repeated command sequences
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanalyze\fR [\fB\-\-min\-count\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-len\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\fR] [\fB\-\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mine shell history for repeated command sequences
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-count\fR \fI<MIN_COUNT>\fR
Minimum repetitions before a sequence is reported
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR [default: 10]
Maximum number of candidates to show
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-len\fR \fI<MAX_LEN>\fR
Longest command sequence to look for
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\fR
Print candidates only; create nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read this history file instead of auto\-detecting one
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  fg analyze \-\-dry
